<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 516.6 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 516.6 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of January 16 raised 516.6 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 346.6 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 112.45 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    14.21 (14.24)	   53.7 (40.6)</p>
<p>    Six months		16.01 (16.08)	  239.2 (49.4)</p>
<p>    12 months		 16.76 (16.90)	   83.2 (62.5)</p>
<p>    24 months		 18.70 (19.02)	  140.5 (194.1)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at 1,550.75 to the U.S. dollar on Monday from 1,551.25 a week earlier and 1,592.5 a year ago.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307 745308</p>
</text>
